Stars help players level up their [[jobs]] in ''[[Free Realms]]'', similar to experience points in traditional role-playing games.<ref>[https://fr.fanbyte.com/wiki/Stars_%28FR%29 Stars] on [https://fr.fanbyte.com/wiki/ ZAM]</ref> Most jobs earn stars by playing [[Mini-Games|minigames]], such as [[combat]] and [[cooking]]. [[Adventurer|Adventurers]] earn stars by collecting in-world exploration coins and completing [[Exploration (Collections)|exploration collections]].<ref>[https://youtu.be/T-gxBo8ImE4?t=1966 2011/3/20 - Rise and Shiny recap: Free Realms] on [https://www.youtube.com YouTube]</ref> Stars are also rewarded for completing [[quests]] in each job's questline. Combat jobs offer repeatable contract quests at certain milestones of combat questlines to help players earn additional stars.

In general, stars earned from quests, collections, and minigames only count towards a specific job. For example, the stars from [[Miner]] quests and [[Mining]] minigames go straight to the Miner job. However, some collections reward wildcard stars that can be used to level any job, such as the [[List of Collections#Archaic|Artifacts]] collections in [[Blackspore Swamp]]. Players that engage in overworld combat also receive stars from mob kills, regardless of the job they're using.<ref>[https://youtu.be/ol27Yw9r_MI?t=39 Free Realms - an experiment (how to level up your adventure a funny way)] on [https://www.youtube.com YouTube]</ref>

